  "aboutTitle": "About this app",
  "aboutBody": "Webcam & Screen Saver uses an Android phone left at home as the camera, and the phone you carry as the viewer. Enter only the home camera IP. Port 8787 and the video path are added for you. An upright phone sends a tall picture. A phone on its side sends a wide picture. On and off commands for home devices run on the home phone.",
  "aboutWindows": "The Windows program can fill the screen as a screensaver. In its settings, Show as background plays the same video behind the desktop icons. Moving the mouse closes the screensaver. The desktop background stays on. Get the installer from GitHub Releases.",
  "privacyBody": "Webcam & Screen Saver does not create a developer account. Video moves only between the home phone and the viewer, over Tailscale or an address you open. The developer server does not store video, accounts, or location history.\n\nCamera permission is used only when this phone is the home camera. Network permission is used to send and receive video. Nearby discovery looks for devices on the same home network.\n\nIf you use Tailscale, sign-in stays in the Tailscale app and follows Tailscale’s policy.\n\nThe GitHub account anyethernet publishes this app.\nPrivacy manager: Kim Judong\nContact: https://github.com/anyethernet"
